WEBVTT

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.940
The Tokugawa army, around 200,000 strong, 
attacked Osaka Castle from every direction

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.310
until the war, later known as 
the Winter Siege of Osaka,

00:00:11.740 --> 00:00:15.490
came to an end, with the Toyotomi 
clan accepting a truce.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.830
The terms of the ceasefire

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.670
guaranteed that Hideyori would not 
be punished for his part in the war,

00:00:24.870 --> 00:00:28.950
and that the Toyotomi clan would keep its domain.

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:34.410
But in return, Osaka Castle's second and third 
lines of defense would be torn down,

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.680
and the outer moat filled in.

00:00:42.440 --> 00:00:46.190
The work was carried out accordingly,

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:51.510
but merely filling a moat would 
not be enough to repair the rift

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:55.610
remaining between the two clans.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:40.100
I can't believe we're destroying the castle, 
which Lord Hideyoshi built, with our own hands.

00:02:40.690 --> 00:02:42.400
Please forgive us...

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:47.890
What's the meaning of this?

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.890
The Toyotomi clan's in charge of the second line!

00:02:50.890 --> 00:02:53.650
But you do not seem to be making any progress.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:58.780
We also have to repair damage the 
main keep sustained in the war.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.030
Yes, and that's why we are 
offering to take over here.

00:03:02.440 --> 00:03:04.450
We can handle it just fine ourselves!

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.830
If we leave it in your hands, who knows 
how many years it will take?

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:11.670
Are you picking a fight?

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.630
That was not my intent,

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:21.260
but if it's a fight you want, you'll get one.

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.050
Now we're talking...

00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:31.670
Hold it right there!

00:03:32.890 --> 00:03:35.020
This is no battlefield.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.990
Stand down, both of you.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:38.480
But...

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:43.240
If you start a fight here, you'll be 
causing trouble for Hideyori.

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:59.750
I can't say I approve of your tactics, either.

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:09.470
West Enclosure     Second Line     Main Keep    East Enclosure 
Third Line 
South Enclosure         Sanada Maru

00:04:07.520 --> 00:04:12.310
Having finished tearing down the third line 
of defense and filling in the outer moat,

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:12.850
Second Line      Main Keep     Second Line

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.100
the Tokugawa clan forcefully undertook

00:04:12.850 --> 00:04:17.270
Main Keep

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:16.440
demolition of the second line, 
the Toyotomi clan's responsibility.

00:04:16.790 --> 00:04:19.600
Furthermore, they also filled in the inner moat,

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:22.570
despite that not being one 
of the ceasefire's terms.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:25.080
What a sad sight...

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:30.900
You must love this castle very much.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.490
I am not the only one who does.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.040
My father did not simply build this castle.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:43.540
He also did his best to ensure the happiness 
of those who lived around it.

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:48.550
And in turn, those people loved him and his castle.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:53.810
That goes for us, as well.

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:57.810
A castle is a pillar of support 
for the warrior's heart.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:03.070
Losing it would be more painful 
than losing one's limbs.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:09.690
Curse that Ieyasu...

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:14.130
This castle is my lord's will to create 
a peaceful land made manifest.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:20.590
No matter what, I shall unite Japan,

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:24.840
and create a world full of smiles!

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:29.350
I hope you continue to support 
me in this endeavor!

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:34.100
Ieyasu should know that himself.

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:37.380
It's sad to see this castle stripped bare...

00:05:37.380 --> 00:05:38.480
Yeah.

00:05:39.250 --> 00:05:41.860
They intend to attack this place again.

00:05:42.770 --> 00:05:44.610
Was that their plan all along?

00:05:45.100 --> 00:05:48.400
Lord Hideyori, we must prepare to face them!

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:51.830
Yukimura...

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.620
What do you think?

00:05:57.130 --> 00:06:00.170
The Tokugawa clan won't leave 
the Toyotomi standing.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:03.870
Next time will be to the death.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:09.220
I believe another war with the 
Tokugawa clan is inevitable.

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:11.710
I agree.

00:06:14.090 --> 00:06:19.060
Once the second line of defense was demolished 
and the inner moat filled in,

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.980
Takatora Todo visited Osaka Castle, 
as the Tokugawa clan's messenger.

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.390
The demands he passed on were as follows:

00:06:26.390 --> 00:06:31.690
all the vagabond samurai that remained in Osaka, 
including Yukimura, were to be exiled,

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.630
and Hideyori was to leave the castle.

00:06:35.030 --> 00:06:37.690
Hideyori, however, refused to comply,

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:42.500
thus signaling an end to the ceasefire 
between the two clans.

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.010
There you are.

00:06:56.460 --> 00:07:00.060
If you go to war again, the Toyotomi 
 clan doesn't stand a chance.

00:07:00.370 --> 00:07:02.020
Knowing that, will you still fight?

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:09.280
This castle reflects the Toyotomi 
clan's current state.

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:14.130
Without its second and third lines of 
defense and its moats filled in,

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:16.790
it cuts a pathetic figure, with only its main keep.

00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:23.040
But there are still people who shower 
this clan with their love and support.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:29.800
I hold dear the people gathered here, 
as though they're my own family.

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.630
Family?

00:07:31.630 --> 00:07:35.970
True, the wind blows in the 
Tokugawa clan's direction.

00:07:36.790 --> 00:07:42.440
However, I will not let it decide 
the fate of the Toyotomi clan.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.730
I shall see to the Toyotomi's future myself.

00:07:54.550 --> 00:07:56.580
What are you doing?

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:57.870
Hurry up.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:58.770
Yes.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:07:59.870
Lady Kai...

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:02.170
There's going to be another war, right?

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:03.100
Yeah.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.650
We'll make lots of delicious food

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:09.250
so you can do your best out there!

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.340
Family, huh?

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:14.860
Sure.

00:08:15.340 --> 00:08:16.760
I'm counting on you.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.060
We're on it.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.020
Let's get to work, girls.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:21.490
Yes!

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:22.610
<i>That's right.</i>

00:08:22.870 --> 00:08:25.980
<i>The people in this castle are my family now.</i>

00:08:25.980 --> 00:08:28.530
<i>I have to keep them safe, no matter what!</i>

00:08:30.160 --> 00:08:35.530
Once Takatora told Ieyasu 
about Hideyori's response,

00:08:35.810 --> 00:08:40.040
Ieyasu ordered feudal lords across the country 
to gather troops at Osaka Castle again.

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:45.540
I'll have to pile up even more stones.

00:08:46.570 --> 00:08:47.590
Stones?

00:08:54.580 --> 00:08:58.880
I've already dug thousands of graves in my heart.

00:09:00.440 --> 00:09:04.010
But I cannot stop here.

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.730
Though I bear the hatred of thousands...

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:11.520
I have to keep going.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:16.450
I must protect the country. 
Otherwise, we'll end up with more graves.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:20.080
Why tell me this?

00:09:24.570 --> 00:09:28.080
Going to war means sacrificing many lives.

00:09:28.240 --> 00:09:34.550
But while I may become an object of hatred, 
that's a cross I'm prepared to bear.

00:09:34.550 --> 00:09:38.090
I believe I understand the purpose of this war.

00:09:39.540 --> 00:09:44.850
People do not value things obtained 
without any pain or sacrifice.

00:09:45.140 --> 00:09:46.280
Exactly.

00:09:46.280 --> 00:09:49.000
To build a long-lasting world of peace,

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.860
we must inflict pain upon this era and ourselves.

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:55.860
And to see that world to fruition,

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:00.550
you must shoulder the pain of your brother's death.

00:10:07.330 --> 00:10:08.120
Yes, sir.

00:10:09.030 --> 00:10:11.810
I shall put an end to the Warring States Era

00:10:11.810 --> 00:10:14.870
by killing Yukimura with my own hands.

00:10:31.730 --> 00:10:33.860
All for the sake of peace, huh?

00:10:36.080 --> 00:10:37.380
Lord Hidetada,

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:39.020
what are you doing here?

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:43.870
O-Oh, it's just you.

00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:46.380
Here to see my father again?

00:10:46.380 --> 00:10:48.720
He must like you a lot.

00:10:49.670 --> 00:10:54.250
Simply looking at that stoic 
mug of yours irritates me.

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:59.590
I bet you think I'm a paper shogun, too.

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:01.010
That I'm a good-for-nothing!

00:11:01.850 --> 00:11:05.010
Is that how you see yourself?

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.140
How could I not?

00:11:07.140 --> 00:11:08.640
I'm a mere figurehead!

00:11:08.640 --> 00:11:11.520
Father makes all the important decisions himself!

00:11:11.520 --> 00:11:14.020
In the Tokugawa clan, where do I even stand?

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.490
To begin with, I don't like warfare.

00:11:17.490 --> 00:11:19.780
I'm not the least bit interested in spoils of war.

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:25.030
How am I supposed to control 
this nation as its shogun?!

00:11:28.590 --> 00:11:30.120
A pacifist?

00:11:30.470 --> 00:11:32.040
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:11:32.380 --> 00:11:33.430
What?

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:37.760
As a pacifist, you should become a splendid shogun,

00:11:37.760 --> 00:11:41.240
who keeps the world from ever returning to chaos.

00:11:41.240 --> 00:11:44.050
As if I could ever play such an important role...

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:48.810
If you do not, all the people who lost their lives 
to war will be unable to rest in peace.

00:11:51.880 --> 00:11:52.820
Hmph!

00:11:52.820 --> 00:11:54.560
Lecturing me now?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:57.290
This is why I can't stand you, Sanada!

00:12:26.630 --> 00:12:27.890
At last,

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:33.250
a massive Tokugawa army began 
its march toward Osaka.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:43.480
I can tell you've already prepared yourself.

00:12:43.480 --> 00:12:45.430
I shall have Lord Ieyasu's head.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:48.370
There is no other way to win this war.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:52.370
The traditional samurai fighting style.

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:53.550
Indeed.

00:12:54.130 --> 00:12:57.740
Break through a massive army, 
to barge into the enemy camp?

00:12:57.740 --> 00:12:59.380
Sounds amusing.

00:13:00.710 --> 00:13:03.240
I shall stake my life on this one spear.

00:13:04.340 --> 00:13:06.780
That is what it means to be a warrior.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:11.000
In the past, the Takeda clan's cavalry 
was thought to be invincible,

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:13.390
but they fell to Oda's gunners.

00:13:14.120 --> 00:13:16.910
And in last winter's war,

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:19.610
the once-impregnable Osaka Castle

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:22.980
was rendered helpless by cannons.

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:29.940
My thinking is that wars fought with swords 
and spears will soon be a thing of the past.

00:13:31.420 --> 00:13:36.710
But that is exactly why I want to fight 
like a warrior to the bitter end!

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:39.370
In this final battle!

00:13:40.570 --> 00:13:42.350
Final, eh?

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:49.460
I wonder what your brother's up to...

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.010
He is no longer any concern of mine.

00:13:58.630 --> 00:14:00.290
The final battle...

00:14:02.850 --> 00:14:04.230
Why don't you just tell him?

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:08.480
Why don't you tell him not to die?

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:10.030
I cannot...

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:12.650
I'm his ninja, after all.

00:14:12.650 --> 00:14:14.170
What are you saying?

00:14:14.170 --> 00:14:20.090
Lord Yukimura's trying to make his last stand 
as a warrior, so I cannot stop him.

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:22.040
How could I?

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:34.370
You love him, don't you? Then you'd 
better make sure to protect him!

00:14:35.200 --> 00:14:40.440
And if you're both alive when the war ends, 
tell him how you feel!

00:14:41.050 --> 00:14:45.520
If he's going to take a stand as a warrior, 
you need only take a stand as a woman!

00:14:50.140 --> 00:14:51.010
Right!

00:15:05.030 --> 00:15:09.130
The Tokugawa army marching on Osaka, 
and the Toyotomi army looking to stop them...

00:15:09.500 --> 00:15:13.280
This marked the beginning of the 
massive war later known as

00:15:13.280 --> 00:15:15.630
the Summer Siege of Osaka.

00:15:31.830 --> 00:15:34.620
Masamune!

00:15:43.860 --> 00:15:44.830
Yukimura!

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:07.400
Lord Yukimura!

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:17.660
The Tokugawa clan may have hundreds 
of thousands of soldiers,

00:16:18.020 --> 00:16:20.410
but it appears they have not a single warrior!

00:16:23.610 --> 00:16:27.170
Thanks to Yukimura and his troops' valiant efforts,

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.670
the Toyotomi army put up a good fight.

00:16:30.110 --> 00:16:33.570
But the enemy's overwhelming numerical advantage

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:37.930
gradually pushed them to the brink.

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:49.070
And in the end,

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:54.350
the Tokugawa army made it to within 
a stone's throw from Osaka Castle.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:05.440
<i>Lord Mitsunari,</i>

00:17:06.470 --> 00:17:10.090
<i>please watch over my final battle.</i>

00:17:11.270 --> 00:17:14.730
Lord Yukimura, how are your wounds?

00:17:14.730 --> 00:17:17.180
Not a problem. I'll be fine.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:20.100
Please don't push yourself.

00:17:20.100 --> 00:17:22.600
In order to win this war, I must.

00:17:23.300 --> 00:17:25.100
Even so, I don't want you to!

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:28.270
What's the matter?

00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.390
You aren't acting like yourself.

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:45.330
Don't disturb them.

00:17:49.290 --> 00:17:51.230
Promise me...

00:17:51.230 --> 00:17:52.250
Promise?

00:17:52.830 --> 00:17:56.260
Once this war ends, take me...

00:17:58.460 --> 00:17:59.510
What's wrong?

00:18:08.710 --> 00:18:12.520
Let's go see the cherry blossoms at Ueda Castle!

00:18:16.900 --> 00:18:18.520
Those cherry blossoms?

00:18:23.540 --> 00:18:24.810
You're right.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:28.290
We should go see them together.

00:18:28.830 --> 00:18:30.210
It's a promise, okay?

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.810
So, Lord Yukimura, you have to 
make it through this alive.

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:34.640
Yes.

00:18:35.260 --> 00:18:36.050
In that case,

00:18:37.160 --> 00:18:39.050
could you hold on to this for me?

00:18:40.430 --> 00:18:43.980
Return it once the war's over.

00:18:45.360 --> 00:18:46.570
It's a promise.

00:18:48.780 --> 00:18:50.310
Lord Yukimura...

00:18:50.990 --> 00:18:51.980
Sure.

00:18:51.980 --> 00:18:53.350
I promise.

00:18:55.640 --> 00:18:58.740
<i>I will protect you, Lord Yukimura.</i>

00:18:58.740 --> 00:19:01.820
<i>I'm your ninja, after all.</i>

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.500
A promise, huh?

00:19:17.070 --> 00:19:19.560
We've made it this far.

00:19:20.120 --> 00:19:22.600
Tomorrow, we must settle things.

00:19:23.790 --> 00:19:25.100
Are you going to kill Yukimura?

00:19:25.420 --> 00:19:28.220
That is the pain I am meant to shoulder.

00:19:28.620 --> 00:19:29.560
Pain?

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.350
Are you not the same?

00:19:32.340 --> 00:19:36.280
You broke the vow you shared with Mitsunari, 
in order to protect the Uesugi clan.

00:19:36.280 --> 00:19:39.220
That is the pain you chose to shoulder.

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:40.350
I see.

00:19:40.760 --> 00:19:41.610
You're right.

00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:44.010
For a peaceful world,

00:19:44.010 --> 00:19:46.870
in which everyone can lead happy lives,

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:51.300
we samurai must take on a painful burden.

00:20:03.670 --> 00:20:05.300
Lady Nene!

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:07.430
It's been a while, Ieyasu.

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:10.900
Is this the last war?

00:20:11.780 --> 00:20:12.690
Yes.

00:20:13.790 --> 00:20:17.690
It will bring about a world full of smiles, right?

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:19.750
Without a doubt.

00:20:23.850 --> 00:20:27.700
Then I'll see for myself, in my lord's stead,

00:20:28.580 --> 00:20:30.700
what the future holds for this world.

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:39.210
You have my word.

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>Episode 11</i>

00:22:04.880 --> 00:22:09.890
<i>The Lofty Castle</i>

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
Sengoku Musou 
High School

00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:45.150
11th Period

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:47.820
Coffee

00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:47.820
Convenience Store

00:23:45.450 --> 00:23:47.820
What the hell, man?

00:23:47.820 --> 00:23:49.690
Transfer to Kyushu?

00:23:49.690 --> 00:23:51.270
Mitsunari's gotta be pulling our leg!

00:23:51.270 --> 00:23:52.730
Yeah, I couldn't believe it.

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:54.620
I was madder than a bull in a china shop.

00:23:54.620 --> 00:23:56.330
Yeah, same here.

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:58.790
If he thinks he can get away with this, 
he's got another thing coming!

00:23:58.790 --> 00:24:00.830
Yeah, let's make him cry uncle.

00:24:01.550 --> 00:24:02.920
"Cry uncle," Kiyomasa?

00:24:03.390 --> 00:24:05.170
Who says that nowadays?

00:24:05.550 --> 00:24:06.420
You guys...

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:08.840
You're like so last century, you know?

00:24:08.840 --> 00:24:09.880
<i>To Be Continued</i>

00:24:09.880 --> 00:24:24.840
<i>Next Episode</i>

00:24:10.620 --> 00:24:14.930
The next massive war is the final battle between 
the Tokugawa and Toyotomi clans.

00:24:15.250 --> 00:24:18.810
Staking his warrior's pride on his spear,

00:24:18.810 --> 00:24:21.310
Yukimura charges through the battlefield.

00:24:21.600 --> 00:24:24.730
Next time: "The Mightiest Warrior in Japan."

00:24:22.480 --> 00:24:24.850
<i>Episode 12 
The Mightiest 
Warrior in Japan</i>
